   "id": "korea-swing",
   "group": "Korea",
   "headline": "KOSPI gives back 3% after Wednesday's 6.6% jump as Samsung's quarter falls short",
   "when": "Wed 28 Oct to Thu 11:20 KST",
   "what": "The KOSPI closed Wednesday at 6,012.44, up 6.63%, after SK hynix reported record quarterly revenue and operating profit and a 2026 shareholder-return programme above ₩100 trillion. On Thursday it was down 3.01% at 5,831.34 by 11:20 after Samsung's third-quarter results came in slightly below analyst expectations. Samsung shares fell 6.61%; SK hynix rose 0.4%.",
   "why": "Korea is your largest exposure after the US and Thailand. This morning your dashboard prices SCBKEQTG at its 26 Oct NAV, and the KOSPI is about 6.9% above its level then, so most of this week's gain isn't in your portfolio value yet. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30. EWY, which you hold directly, is already priced at today's level.",
