   "when": "Wed 28 Oct · 14:00 ET",
   "what": "The FOMC voted 10–2 to leave its target range unchanged. Lisa Cook and Beth Hammack wanted a quarter-point increase. The statement says inflation remains elevated and economic activity is expanding at a strong pace. It says the Committee will gather more information before settling on the stance needed to return inflation to 2%.",
