   "what": "The Monetary Policy Committee voted unanimously to keep the policy rate at 1.00%; one member was absent. It expects growth of 2.4% in 2026 and 2.1% in 2027, helped by exports and investment tied to technology and AI. Headline inflation is forecast at 2.1% in 2026 and should rise into early 2027 because of energy prices and El Niño.",
